{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "During the winter in Pasadena, the temperature, in ${F}^{∘}$, $t$ hours after $9$ a.m. can be modeled by the function $T(t)=50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}).$ Find the average temperature during the period from $9$ a.m. to $9$ p.m." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Since the function is valid starting from $9$ A.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,12].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12-0}{\\int }_{0}^{12}(50+14\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{12}(50t-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi t}{12}))|}_{0}^{12} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(50\\cdot 12-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 12}{12}))-(50\\cdot 0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{12}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(0-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[(600-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{168}{\\pi }\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}[\\frac{600\\pi +168}{\\pi }+\\frac{168}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{12}(\\frac{600\\pi +336}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =\\frac{600\\pi +336}{12\\pi } \\\\  & ≈{58.9}^{∘}F.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3289" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65952f4538c3b42149c35a6dc2b429cb4be88cfe356c407496c72e623084c916"} {"question" "q-3289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "{50.0}^{∘}F"] ["math" "{52.1}^{∘}F"] ["math" "{56.5}^{∘}F"] ["math" "{58.9}^{∘}F"] ["math" "{61.2}^{∘}F"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3289" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{58.9}^{∘}F"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the number $c>0$ such that the average value of $f(x)=9+8x-3{x}^{2}$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-3.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}\\,{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}\\,{\\int }_{0}^{c}(9+8x-3{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c}(9x+4{x}^{2}-{x}^{3}){|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -3 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(9c+4{c}^{2}-{c}^{3})-(0)] \\\\ -3 & =9+4c-{c}^{2} \\\\ {c}^{2}-4c-12 & =0 \\\\ (c+2)(c-6) & =0 \\\\ c & =-2,\\,6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, since $c>0,$ we conclude that $c=6$ only." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3293" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65952f4538c3b42149c35a6dc2b429cb4be88cfe356c407496c72e623084c916"} {"question" "q-3293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "2"] ["math" "4"] ["math" "5"] ["math" "6"] ["math" "7"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-3293" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "6"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-30872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=-6{x}^{2}+14x-5$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-30872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(-6{x}^{2}+14x-5)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ 0 & ={\\frac{1}{c}(-2{x}^{3}+7{x}^{2}-5x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ 0 & =\\frac{1}{c}[(-2{c}^{3}+7{c}^{2}-5c)-0] \\\\ 0 & =-2{c}^{2}+7c-5 \\\\ 2{c}^{2}-7c+5 & =0 \\\\ (c-1)(2c-5) & =0 \\\\ c & =1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-30872" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65952f4538c3b42149c35a6dc2b429cb4be88cfe356c407496c72e623084c916"} {"question" "q-30872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-30872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2},\\,5"] ["math" "-\\frac{5}{2},\\,1"] ["math" "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{2},\\,5"] ["math" "\\frac{5}{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-30872" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1,\\,\\frac{5}{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-316309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/assets/1c69b5a43e445861a728fcd8faed9e89b3bcb61141ad35d99e60f2a43983244d.png)\n\nThe graph of the function $f(x),$ which is defined on $[-2,9],$ is shown above. It consists of three line segments and the arc of the semi-circle centered at $(5,0)$ with radius $3.$ \n\nFind the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of $f(x)$ on $[0,8].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-316309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The average value of a function on a given interval $[a,b]$ is \n\n$$\n{f}_{\\text{avg}}=\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nUsing the additive property of the definite integral, we write\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x={{{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{-{A}_{1}}+{{{\\int }_{2}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x}_{⏟}}_{{A}_{2}}.\n$$\n\nThe 1st integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [0,2].$ The corresponding region is a right triangle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{1} & =\\frac{1}{2}bh \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 2\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince the region lies below the $x$-axis, we have \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{A}_{1}=-2.\n$$\n\nThe 2nd integral represents the signed area between the curve and the $x$-axis, where $x\\in [2,8].$ The corresponding region is a semi-circle, so we find the area using the formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}_{2} & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi {r}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\pi \\cdot {3}^{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{8}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-{A}_{1}+{A}_{2} \\\\  & =-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, using the formula for the average value, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{8-0}\\cdot (-2+\\frac{9\\pi }{2}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}+\\frac{9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{-4+9\\pi }{16} \\\\  & =\\frac{9\\pi -4}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-316309" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65952f4538c3b42149c35a6dc2b429cb4be88cfe356c407496c72e623084c916"} {"question" "q-316309" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-316309" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{9\\pi}{16}-\\frac{1}{4}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-344695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the average value ${f}_{\\text{avg}}$ of the function $f(x)=\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)$ on the interval $[0,\\frac{\\pi }{3}].$ Do not round the answer.\n\n${f}_{\\text{avg}}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-344695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Applying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{(\\frac{\\pi }{3}-0)}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{3}{\\pi }(-\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)}{3})|}_{0}^{\\pi /3} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }[(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot (-1))-(-\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot 1)] \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }(\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{\\pi }\\cdot \\frac{2}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-344695" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "65952f4538c3b42149c35a6dc2b429cb4be88cfe356c407496c72e623084c916"} {"question" "q-344695" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"} {"question" "q-344695" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{2}{\\pi}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14031367/state.json" "file_sha256" "c142c3aa765d0ab791cc5d63c5efa8735eb5f0295fdaff3e9f7ba673abbf1066"}] "usage" {"q-3293" []} "basis" 1213 "retractions" [[17592186101296 :question/problem "Find the number $c > 0$ such that the average value of $f(x) = 9 + 8x - 3x^{2}$ on the interval $[0, c]$ is equal to $-3$."]] "immutable_answers" [17592186099378 17592186099379 17592186099380 17592186099381 17592186099382] "immutable_fields" [[17592186099377 :answer-field/correct] [17592186099377 :answer-field/id] [17592186099377 :answer-field/key] [17592186099377 :answer-field/type]] "no_history" []}
